&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of experience with order entry and email handling in a high-volume environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2+ years of customer service experience in a call center or high-volume support environment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1+ year of logistics coordination experience, including domestic LTL/freight scheduling and documentation (BOLs)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written and verbal communication skills (email and phone), including knowledge of professional email etiquette&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A customer-first mindset, with the patience and judgment to calm tense situations and see issues through to resolution&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A track record of managing a daily workload with about 90% autonomy, bringing proposed solutions when you raise problems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to keep your speed and accuracy steady as tasks get more complex&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort with tech stacks (ERP, WMS, or logistics platforms) and investigating mismatches between system records and physical inventory&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong attention to detail, a positive attitude, and a team-player mindset suited to a fast-paced startup&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Must pass a customer service assessment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Preferred&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
