&lt;li&gt;Partner with the marketing and events team early in planning to scope security requirements and assess risk for internal, customer-facing, and executive-attended events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and execute end-to-end security plans, including site assessments, guard and vendor staffing, and credentialing/access plans.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as the on-site point of contact before, during, and after events to manage issues in real time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Travel to supervise on-site security for events and support physical security operations at Verkada locations, as needed.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support daily physical security operations, including access administration, investigations, and incident response.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct ongoing security audits to identify and close gaps in physical security coverage at remote locations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate with the executive protection and physical security team on operations outside of the event calendar.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor internal and external threats to identify and assess potential threats.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produce threat briefs ahead of high-profile events, executive travel, or company announcements that draw attention.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3-5+ years of experience in corporate or physical security, ideally with direct experience planning security for corporate events, VIP visits, or high-profile gatherings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort managing both live events and daily physical security operations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to turn vague or incomplete requirements into a solid, actionable security plan.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communication skills across a wide range of stakeholders, from event planners to executives to on-site security guards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Calm, detail-oriented execution under pressure, especially with credentialing and vendor logistics.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with access control and video security systems is a plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Relevant certification (PSP, CPP, or similar) is a nice-to-have, not required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
