&lt;p&gt;This is a very exciting opportunity to join Verkada’s growing People team. You will report directly to the SVP/Head of People. We are seeking a forward-thinking and operationally strong leader to lead all aspects of the employee lifecycle and People service delivery. This role is responsible for building and optimizing scalable People processes that support a growing and high-performing workforce. This is an opportunity to move from functional leadership into enterprise impact.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are committed to a thriving in-office culture. This role requires that you be on-site at our office in San Mateo, CA, 5 days a week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Will Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People Leadership: &lt;/strong&gt;Manage and continuously improve core People operations, including onboarding, employee records, offboarding, and People service delivery.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People Operations:&lt;/strong&gt; Design and implement scalable People processes, policies, and workflows that support high-performing and rapidly growing teams.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People Technology &amp;amp; Systems&lt;/strong&gt;: Design and oversee the People technology stack (e.g., Workday and benefits systems), driving automation, ensuring a seamless employee experience, whilst ensuring accurate data integrity and reporting.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Employee Lifecycle Management: &lt;/strong&gt;Oversee the end-to-end employee journey with an emphasis on efficiency, employee experience, and automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;People Analytics: &lt;/strong&gt;Design and deliver meaningful workforce analytics to measure the impact of People programs and inform organizational health, workforce planning, and executive decision-making.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits and compensation:&lt;/strong&gt; Lead benefit programs globally and partner with our head of compensation to scale compensation infrastructure.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compliance &amp;amp; Risk Management:&lt;/strong&gt; Ensure People processes comply with all local labor laws, internal policies and various audit standards.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Cross-Functional Leadership:&lt;/strong&gt; Partner with leadership across Legal, Finance, Security, IT and other departments to align people programs with broader business goals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process &amp;amp; Policy Development:&lt;/strong&gt; Establish and maintain scalable People policies, SOPs, and workflows that align with business goals and operational standards.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Qualifications&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Bachelor&#39;s degree required; advanced degree or MBA preferred.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;10–15 years of progressive experience in the People space, with 5+ years in a senior operations leadership role.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of labor laws, HR compliance, and operational risk management.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience in implementing and optimizing HR systems such as Workday or similar platforms.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
