&lt;p&gt;You can look at all kinds of communities to see our platform’s impact in the world. It&#39;s the retailer that uses our agentic AI to deter theft before it happens. The warehouse that uses AI-powered alerts to make sure its team is protected on the floor with proper PPE. The school that’s alerted to a threat in real-time and triggers a lockdown in seconds, not minutes. We’re rapidly scaling this impact: today, more than 2 million Verkada devices are deployed across 170+ countries.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a rockstar product lawyer who has a knack for creative problem solving and a desire to make an impact. You will be a cornerstone member of the Product Legal team and will be joining Verkada’s fast growing Legal team. This role reports into Verkada’s AGC for Product.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate will have experience advising product and hardware engineering teams on legal issues arising throughout the product development lifecycle, &lt;em&gt;especially those relating to regulatory compliance, government procurement requirements, and marketing&lt;/em&gt;. You will also have expertise in one or more of the following areas: (1) domestic and international regulatory compliance for connected devices; (2) licensing and regulatory issues related to commercial alarm products and monitoring services, including fire safety systems; and/or (3) federal regulatory requirements for government contractor supply chain and dual use technologies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you enjoy building from the ground up, this role is for you! We are committed to a thriving in-office culture. This role requires that you be on-site at our office in Austin, TX 5 days a week.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You&#39;ll Do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be a legal go-to for the product, engineering, supply chain, and marketing teams, advising them on all legal aspects related to Verkada’s product offerings, including their development, marketing, sale, and compliance with applicable laws&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Advise company leadership about legal issues involving Verkada’s product offerings, help design and implement compliance programs, and provide practical legal risk mitigation strategies across multiple jurisdictions&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Simplify and distill complex, evolving legal frameworks into guidance that accelerates—not slows—product delivery&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Uplevel our product launch process and protocols to ensure new product offerings are adequately protected by and compliant with applicable laws and regulations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Serve as a subject matter expert on product-related regulatory issues, including in relevant import/export and government procurement laws (e.g., NDAA/TAA/BAA), and support systematic documentation of our ongoing compliance with those laws&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop global internal controls, risk monitoring, and audit frameworks for OFAC, ITAR and emerging AI-related export controls that scale with the business&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor new and emerging developments in applicable worldwide regulations and laws, and identify potential impacts on current and future Verkada product offerings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What You Bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;J.D. degree from an ABA-approved law school or equivalent and a member of at least one state bar association in good standing&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;6+ years of legal experience comprising a combination of regulatory, IP, product counseling, marketing, and general transactional work (preferably with at least 2 years of in house experience)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience advising multinational, complex fast-growing global companies, preferably with respect to both hardware and software product offerings&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience developing and implementing compliance programs and policies for hardware and software products, including alarms products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expertise in one or more of the following areas: (1) Federal procurement requirements for hardware and software (e.g. FedRAMP, FIPs, NDAA); (2) licensing and regulatory compliance for alarm products, including fire alarms; and/or (3) domestic and EU regulatory compliance for connected devices&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Excellent legal and business judgment with the ability to provide practical, concise advice&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to manage multiple projects, prioritize and meet deadlines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
