&lt;li&gt;Be the primary business partner to several of our senior leaders&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Drive financial planning and budgeting as the accountable owner for key portions of our several hundred million dollar budget&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Define the management dashboard / key operating metrics that help us understand the health of our business, and generate deep insights around our performance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Identify opportunities to improve resource allocation and operating efficiency, and work cross-functionally to tackle critical change projects to realize these opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help us operate the business at the next level of scale through better tooling, self-serve automation, and internal processes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We’re looking for:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;2-6+ years of top tier professional experience.&lt;/strong&gt; You’re coming to us from a Strategic Finance, Business Operations, Sales Operations, FP&amp;amp;A, or other highly analytical role at a fast growing company, and may have begun your career in investing, management consulting, and/or investment banking.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;High analytical horsepower paired with strong modeling and data skills.&lt;/strong&gt; You can effortlessly translate business concepts and frameworks to well structured spreadsheet models, and have the analytical toolkit to autonomously generate insights through data. Fluency in database concepts, SQL, and the latest AI tools is a big plus… you use AI to supercharge (not substitute for) your strong technical capabilities!&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Attention to detail &lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;and&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt; strong strategic instincts.&lt;/strong&gt; You are meticulous in ensuring your and others’ output is precise and error-free, but pair this with a strong sense for 80/20 to know when things “pass the smell test” and what is critical vs. secondary to an answer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;A growth mindset and comfort with ambiguity.&lt;/strong&gt; You are comfortable working in a fast-paced startup environment that will require you to create structure out of ambiguity, manage often competing priorities, and pivot quickly when circumstances change.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Excellent communication and partnership skills.&lt;/strong&gt; You can effectively engage with a diverse array of stakeholders ranging from sales reps to engineers, and build the credibility, relationships, and buy-in necessary to strike the delicate balance between partnering and constructive challenging that this role requires.&lt;/li&gt;
